// =============================================================================
// Task Service - Distributed Task Queue Management
// =============================================================================
// Purpose: Manages the ordered task queue for agent nodes. This is the central
// orchestration service that distributes work (VM operations) to agent nodes.
//
// Communication:
// - gRPC streaming for task subscription (agent receives tasks in real-time)
// - Unary RPC for task CRUD operations (frontend/director creates/manages tasks)
//
// Key Concepts:
// - Task types: VM lifecycle (create, start, stop, delete) and advanced operations
//   (migrate, snapshot, clone, export/import OVA)
// - Task status: PENDING -> IN_PROGRESS -> COMPLETED/FAILED/CANCELLED
// - Sequence numbers ensure ordered processing
// - Priority allows important tasks to be processed first
// - Superseded tasks: newer operations can invalidate older pending ones
// =============================================================================

